texts={'r1.txt': '# REVIEW_VERDICT_R1P: GO AFTER FIXES (fixed packet 841f0637, archive p_0a4d6fc3 db2a80b7; FIX3.md+FIX3.diff reviewed; snapshot 1ec4a936 alone: NO-GO, see 2)\nEvidence copies: /scratch/jjyeung/orch_n30/review_r1p/work (fix3/ frozen 15:46Z, SHA256SUMS OK; scripts units.py, impl.py, resume.py).\n1. HIGH, blocks proof (snapshot and fix3). The proof receipt can never PASS: p.py defines temporary_paths (fix3 out/proof/p.py:196) but never calls it; checks at :263 lack it; :287-289 require it -> FAIL; s.sh:37 also refuses. Cause: make_proof.py:61 replaces the anchor "result.update(checks=dict(empty_root=", which only exists after :62 creates it (grep count in work/proof_parent.py = 0). test_packet.py:196 only greps the name. Fix: call it after `args = command(...)`; add a test that a receipt built by main() holds all 8 checks.\n2. HIGH, snapshot only; FIX3 fixes it. d07c3bd5 keeps H1\'s s1_pool implementation fingerprint; snapshot tree\'s s1_pool.implementation() differs (carrier_c1_data/run, type_mix) -> s1_routing.py:221 would refuse at Orchard. FIX3 88bd3399: my impl.py run on the code3 tree gives EQUAL; only implementation and the 3 room sources differ from eac5f9f0; I reproduced d07c3bd5 from eac5f9f0 with project().\n3. MEDIUM, unit-bound path (inactive now). vehicle_p.py:52-53 fails required_families if cm, ft or in < 100; ruling 1440Z says such a unit is named missing on P. In the 2,000-row slice I find faithful cm 0/633, in 12/678, ft 204/689, so a bound faithful slice will likely FAIL every proof. Also, while units are unbound, absent_on_p (vehicle_p.py:15-22) omits units.\n4. MEDIUM, names. p.py program() adds argv `-m student_pilot.loader_audit`, visible in ps on the shared advanced node, while the inherited kit keeps argv opaque (b/i.py). Inherited from H1-1: t.tar member names rk/revsi.py, scripts/student_benchmark_gpu.sh and configs/student_benchmark_eval_v1.json (kept in 0700 dirs). Orchestrator ruling. Job name a15_cot_ap29c71287 OK; e.txt, bundle and KH names are opaque hex.\n5. LOW. The diff_against_h1_1.json baseline (work/reference/configs/h1_1.json, 998f3645) is not deployed H1-1: deployed over.json pins selection eac5f9f0, vqa c95023e4 and 3 exports; the reference has f232d416, bfabb1f0 and 9. diff_against_deployed.json is correct.\n6. PASS item 3 (diff_against_deployed). Changes: S1 off (faithful_own_camera_rows) and S2 off (routing_pose_targets, key kept); scheduled sampling = D0 (max_own 0, force None); own run 29c71287 with its output and prep dirs; v6 d.json; type_mix; s1_routing selection. Also changed: route_table room -> direct and s1_route_policy table; both are needed, because s1_routing.py:268 then defers legacy room programs. Unchanged: steps 1000, milestones [100,200], stop 200, exports 3, optimizer, init m544, mix 64/128/64/32 (world 4).\n7. PASS item 1. Producer receipt is byte-equal (9fddc043); I hashed rows.sqlite myself (0608dd98). ground_rows, s1_pool, s1_admission and s1_routing are byte-equal to b01ce449. Against the H1 tree, only carrier_c1_data and carrier_c1_run differ, plus the new type_mix, loader_audit and vehicle_p. My recount over all 195,471 rows matches 10 families: direction 49901, facing 34958, counting 11366, totals 9303, size 9778, relative_distance 20665, appearance 27791, box 3813, route 8894, first_seen 7076. Both refusals reproduce: all 1532 recovery rows have not_seen (ground_rows.py:81-82); units 216 pass, 1784 fail agrees() (:89-92).\n8. PASS item 4, LOW note. Quotas are opt-in; bound() returns None when absent. The cap is 4*eligible*100//steps; quotas sum to 6400 and 12800; direction is 32.89; recovery and units (3.87) go proportionally to the 4 routing cells. My resume.py: resumed tails at k=1, 137 and 999 equal the full plan; at-cap populations reach max repeat 4. The OFF test is real (b01ce449 vs candidate tree, 4 ranks equal) but narrow: tiny_worker never passes type_mix or uses the patched Rows.\n9. LOW. Camera routing caps are unmeasured locally. prepare raises "Insufficient eligible rows" unless legacy camera populations are >= 4635, 4033 and 3183 for cells 18.54, 16.13 and 12.73; this fails closed. absolute_distance has 11728 rows (needs 4150).\n10. PASS item 5, LOW note. p.py derives from a_8c74b291 (I decoded and diffed both). It has no --gres, sets CUDA \'\' and checks GPUs/partition, uses the kit-pinned bwrap and binaries hashed at run time, keeps the 0700 walk, checkpoint_space disk plan and loader audit, and stops at prepare_only. It runs mode p for rank 0 only, like its parent. -c 48 --mem=800G may pend beside main\'s jobs on advanced.\n11. Tests: 21/21 pass in my copy.\nRequired before submit: fix 1 and re-seal. Fix 3 before binding units. Rule on 4.\n', 'r2.txt': "# REVIEW_VERDICT_R1P2: GO AFTER FIXES (config 782f303d; snap_782f303d archive 42bbcbb2 and live fix-5 archive 21e1ec60, item 4 included)\nReviewer: review_r1p2 (Devin, Claude Opus), trinity-1-3, 16:15-16:45Z. Evidence: /scratch/jjyeung/orch_n30/review_r1p2/work (s5 = snapshot copy, live = r1_pkt copy at 16:37:53Z, both SHA256SUMS OK; census.py/out, oneline.py, fb_*/ and tests_*.log).\nOnly finding 1 needs a code fix. It blocks the routing-prefix census, not the proof's gates. If the orchestrator takes the ScanNet++ v1 share from another source, proof 1 is GO on archive 42bbcbb2 or 21e1ec60, pinned by SHA (finding 2).\n1. MEDIUM, fix-5 item 2 does not work. In production the routing absolute-distance census by prefix will report every row as `unknown`. `loader_audit.row_metadata` reads `routing.provenance.canonical`, then top-level `provenance.canonical`. Staged routing rows carry `routing.canonical` and have no top-level provenance (carrier_c1_routing.py c1_row :714-728). `arkit` also never matches the canonical name `arkitscenes/` (ALIAS :733). My probe with c1_row-shaped rows gave unknown for scannetpp/, scannetppv2/, scannet/ and arkitscenes/. test_audit_draw_breakdown passes only because it feeds raw-source rows (`provenance={'canonical':..}`). Fix: read `raw['canonical']` first and match `arkitscenes/`, then test on c1_row-shaped rows. The fix changes loader_audit.py, so rebind and re-seal the selection fingerprint. Nothing gates on this census, so it fails silently rather than closed.\n2. MEDIUM, provenance. Three archives share the name p_1130b378.tar and identity 782f303d: snapshot 42bbcbb2, live 21e1ec60, and my rebuild from the snapshot's sources, a9bd0b77. They differ only in u.py (tools/unit_binding.py) and sums.txt. t.tar and every other member are byte-equal, and the tree equals the archive's. The config identity does not cover u.py, and no proof path calls u.py (jb.sh, s.sh, p.py, p_125c4c87.sh). snap_782f303d is not a clean freeze: its rebind.py, unit_binding.py and test_packet.py are dated 16:25Z, after its FIX5.md and tests.log (16:23Z), and hold half-finished item-4 code. Its sources therefore cannot rebuild its archive, and its suite gives 27/28 (KeyError s1_routing.py in the packing test). The live copy passes 28/28. Fix: the proof submission names the archive SHA it uses.\n3. PASS, finding 1 of the first review. p.py:262-263 calls temporary_paths after command(), and :288-290 fails the receipt unless all eight checks are present and PASS. s.sh:37-38 asserts each of the eight. test_main_builds_receipt_with_all_evaluated_checks passes in both copies: it runs the real main(), calls temporary_paths once and writes eight PASS checks. Its fixture mocks command(), program() and execute(), and it fabricates the four checks the audit supplies.\n4. PASS, v7 binding. rows.sqlite hashes to 210b2534 and receipt.json to 8091154c. The archive's d.json (4e539365) pins d.db 210b2534 and the receipt copy 8091154c, and config streams.vqa pins that d.json. My recount over all 204,413 rows: 431 traced room rows (pool r1_room_traced), all admitted by room_trace. away_opp has 8,511 rows (easy 3,664, medium 2,665, hard 2,182), all with facing=away. Direction (49,901) and counting (11,366) equal the first review's counts; facing 43,469 = 34,958 + 8,511. Size is 0 and direction 3,117 = 3,289 - 172. Room 172 = cap 431*4*100//1000. Rerunning the packet's main rebind reproduces 782f303d and run key 125c4c87. Each fallback ran as one command with rc=0. Room 0 gives room 0 and direction 3,289 (identity cfdb1b00). Away excluded gives facing eligible 34,958 with 8,511 excluded (identity 3d056b29).\n5. PASS, room predicate. It admits 431/431 traced rows. It refuses all 571 one-line rows, even with pool forced to r1_room_traced. It refuses all 431 rows under each of my 15 mutants: frame 33, frame 0, no relation, two relations, digit or spelled number, area line, wrong pool, bad pin, no Seen line, non-numeric answer, trailing text, no relation keyword, leading Locate line, extra digit in a Seen line. ground_rows, s1_pool, s1_admission, s1_routing and s1_exclusions are byte-equal to b01ce449. Against snap_841f0637, the tree differs only in type_mix, vehicle_p and loader_audit.\n6. PASS, units. Units are unbound at 0 cents and listed under absent_on_P. Units under 100 go to missing_units and absent_on_P, not to missing. The allowlist defaults to ft. dose = min(cents, 4*eligible*100//1000), and the rest of the 6,400 cents goes pro rata to the four program cells, by largest remainders. Item 4 is off unless --pack-unit-slice is given with four pins. pack_slice adds only events and frame pins and refuses a changed answer (test). The s1_routing SHA 5c8cd973 it hard-codes equals b01ce449's. FIX5 and R1P_PACKET now name units_p_slice_v3 (747 rows: ft 683, in 64), per ORCH NOTE 1605Z.\n7. PASS, names. The loader audit runs as `$PILOT_VENV/bin/python -B - $X` with X=$AS/ap/$K, and its code arrives by heredoc. All new names are opaque hex (p_125c4c87.sh, i_/x_1130b378, ap/1130b378/{c,d,r,s,v}.json, s_22b44165, a15_cot_ap125c4c87). The one name with a project word, benchmark_scene_exclusions.json, is inherited (H1 fx/k, 841f0637).\n8. PASS, selection. Against FIX3's 88bd3399, r.json differs only in the implementation fingerprints of type_mix.py and vehicle_p.py (fix 4) and loader_audit.py (fix 5). s1_pool.implementation() equals r.json on 841f0637, a6b70ef2 and 782f303d. q.json reports non_room_equal, 586 removed and 82,598 selected. Against 841f0637, the config differs only in identity and run pins, the vqa store (v6 to v7), room 172 / direction 3,117, units_allowlist [ft] and exclude_qid_suffix null. Routing cells and every other entry are unchanged. I did not recheck d07c3bd5, which FIX3 superseded.\n9. LOW. With units bound, absent_on_p names only units under 100. An allowlist-excluded unit with 100 or more rows would go undrawn without being named; harmless now that in has 64 rows. s.sh gates with Python `assert` under plain `python3 -B`, so PYTHONOPTIMIZE in the operator's environment would disable every gate (inherited pattern; `-I` or explicit raises would close it).\nNot checked: Orchard staging, real RGB, production routing populations, the v3 half-extent clearance itself.\n", 'r3.txt': "# REVIEW_VERDICT_R1P3: GO (archive p_c5f3847d.tar sha256 888027436a99cfec360959c46f4271222e4c029f5d36eb9870fea4f669231029; config d8b03fd14db01af4def4a0cfd9a49d16ec492d9a3c6b0c56977f7f22b79f705a; run key 26cc98b7)\nReviewer: review_r1p3 (Devin, Claude Opus), trinity-1-3, 17:08-17:18Z. Evidence: /scratch/jjyeung/orch_n30/review_r1p3/work (f6 = snap_f719b05f copy, f7 = r1_pkt copy 17:10:39Z, SHA256SUMS OK for both; ar5/ar6/ar7 extracted archives; gprobe.py, prefix_probe.py, tests_*.log, fb7_main).\nBefore the Orchard proof, the drivers must be repinned to the new identity (finding 7). That step changes no packet code.\n1. PASS, fix 6 deriver. validate_evidence uses only g.read_pin/identity/digest and d.contract. On the deriver's READY kit, inherited g.check(kit,{},'p') passes when only persistent_launch is stubbed. Across 15 evidence mutants plus a re-pin without cfg.admission, g.check and the deriver refuse the same 15, and the deriver also refuses a foreign 4.json config_sha256 that g.check accepts. The deriver omits g.check's slot, version and source-seal predicates. Those predicates bind packet and H bytes, not evidence, and g.check accepts the derived kit. The deriver needs no SLURM variable. The test's audit hook and its r8/persistent_launch profile guard both pass in my copy. The modules it loads (g, i, v, q0, d) have no side effects at import, and the deriver sets dont_write_bytecode.\n2. PASS, fix 6 job path. f719b05f differs from snapshot 42bbcbb2 only in d.py, u.py and sums.txt. u.py (c376dc31) equals the live fix-5 u.py that review_r1p2 reviewed. BASE_RUNTIME and the path substitution are unchanged, and the test's b/ and job.sh files are byte-equal. job.sh:16 still runs `python3 -I b/g.py $ROOT p` in the job environment before r8 and r.sh.\n3. PASS, fix 7 census. I ran 4 datasets x 4 scenes through the packet's c1_row (sha 6da7cebc, JSON round-tripped, no top-level provenance). The fix-7 loader gives the exact prefixes scannetpp/, scannetppv2/, scannet/ and arkitscenes/; the fix-6 loader gives 16/16 unknown. The test builds its rows with the same frozen c1_row.\n4. PASS, fix 7 threshold. 1/100 and 10/1000 PASS; 2/100, 11/1000 and 1/1 FAIL. A FAIL sets a.json to FAIL and raises. p.py requires all 8 checks PASS, and s.sh asserts loader_audit PASS. 0/0 passes this check, but absolute_distance is a required routing family (vehicle_p.ROUTING), so the family gate catches it.\n5. PASS, PYTHONOPTIMIZE. s.sh runs `env -u PYTHONOPTIMIZE python3 -I -B -`. My probe with PYTHONOPTIMIZE=2: `python -I -c 'assert False'` exits rc=1, and without -I it exits rc=0. The proof script and every jb.sh python call also use -I.\n6. PASS, scope. ground_rows, s1_pool, s1_admission, s1_routing and s1_exclusions are byte-equal to b01ce449. The trees differ from f719b05f only in loader_audit.py. d.py, p.py, q.py, qp.py, v.py, u.py and b0.json are unchanged. jb.sh and the proof script differ only by store and run key. s.sh differs by those keys plus -I.\n7. MEDIUM, operational. r1_ops/work/drv still pins 782f303d and 1130b378 (fixture_b/BINDING.json, dv1.sh, ev1.sh, evidence_body.py and 19 other files). evidence_body attests review_r1p and review_r1p2, which covered 782f303d. Fix 7 changed the identity, contract (f37ca476 to b5772ac9), run key, bundle and kit (i_ and x_c5f3847d) and archive. Repin and retest the drivers against d8b03fd1, and cite this verdict.\n8. LOW, config. The config differs from 782f303d in more fields than the brief allows, though every change follows mechanically from the new loader_audit.py:\n   - selection fingerprint: s1_routing.selection.sha256 78d01f89 to 5cf172c4, and its catalog key;\n   - tree: code.sha256 (tree 5e1514ef);\n   - store key 1130b378 to c5f3847d: paths of streams.vqa (d.json 4e539365 to 847b2813, only its embedded paths; d.db stays 210b2534), s1_route_policy.table.path and s1_routing.selection.path;\n   - run key 125c4c87 to 26cc98b7: output and preparation_output;\n   - admission path and sha, which sit outside the identity.\n   type_mix (room 172, direction 3,117, units [ft] at 0, exclude null), recipe, route-table sha and every other field are equal.\n9. PASS, reproduction. I reran the packet's main rebind in my copy. It reproduces d8b03fd1, run key 26cc98b7, byte-equal config.json and BINDING.json, and an archive of 888027436 (non_room_equal, 586 removed, 82,598 selected). I did not rerun the two fallbacks under fix 7.\n10. PASS, seal. The live SHA256SUMS was resealed at 17:10:47Z; only FIX7.diff gained a log tail. All 33 entries verified OK at 17:14Z. The archive sha matches SHA256SUMS, R1P_PACKET.md, OPERATOR.json and REVIEW_REQUEST.json, and no stale 782f303d, 1130b378 or 125c4c87 reference remains.\n11. PASS, tests. My f6 copy passes 3+31 tests, and my f7 copy 3+34 (p1cpu, Python 3.12). /usr/bin/python3 on trinity-1-3 is 3.6 and cannot run them. LOW: a test run rewrites PRE_SUBMISSION, UNIT_CANDIDATE and UNIT_PACKING_CHECK with temporary paths, so a test run inside the sealed packet would break its SHA256SUMS.\nNot checked: production H, Orchard staging, real RGB, production routing populations, and the fix-7 fallbacks.\n", 'r4.txt': '# REVIEW_VERDICT_R1P4: GO (archive p_6f8ed106.tar sha256 def1e1f2b1153328b024209e69fcbb71f2dd556b7376eacb836d40bb66d9845f; config 2c67f1f25114ab1324cee10b796e86afc79d01999ad3881860ab35710e7fee5d; run key 78d0a06c)\nReviewer: review_r1p4 (Devin, Claude Opus), trinity-1-3, 18:35-19:00Z. Evidence: /scratch/jjyeung/orch_n30/review_r1p4/work (f8 = snap_2c67f1f2 copy; ar7/ar8 = extracted proof-1/proof-2 archives; chk_pack.py, chk_fps.py, jdiff.py, probe.sh, tests_f8.log). The tests needed 54 MB of small work/ inputs (records, reference, kit, input.tar and four JSON files), so I copied those too.\n1. PASS, packing. My own check over all 747 rows: every supplied field has the same value as in the slice; packing adds only events and student_input; qid order is unchanged. For all 747 rows, events equal sealed ground_rows.pack(). I rechecked all 23,904 pins against frame_map 17aa3e9e myself. I also recomputed fps from frame_rates 36ae882f (529 by scene, 218 dataset-uniform), total_num_frames from frame_plan 7cc01f36 (the 290 d3 rows use the lower bound), timestamps, question and options. bad=0.\n2. LOW, wording. "Byte for byte" holds per value, not per line: 0 of 747 slice lines are in canonical form, and u.gz holds the re-encoded packed bytes (d7c3206c), not the slice bytes (5f9383fa).\n3. PASS, predicates. ground_rows, s1_pool, s1_admission, s1_routing and s1_exclusions are byte-equal to b01ce449. t.tar differs from proof 1 only in loader_audit.py. q.py, d.py, qp.py, p.py, v.py and b0.json are unchanged. Against proof 1, r.json only adds source U_Faithful (ELIGIBLE, 747 retained) and changes the loader_audit hash and the manifest pin. selected_rows goes from 82,598 to 83,345.\n4. PASS, units. Units 100 cents with allowlist [ft]: 683 ft eligible, cap 273 cents (4 x 683 / 1000 = 2.732). absent_on_P names units/in (64) and units/cm (0). Sealed type_mix.py:161 drops non-allowlisted units, and :164 refuses unit rows from outside the bound u.gz sha. Program cells are 1825/1588/1253/1634, which sum to 6300; with units, the total is 6400 (64.00).\n5. PASS, fail-closed path to Orchard. q.py --unit-binding reruns sealed s1_pool.prepare on the staged u.gz. It checks the JSONL sha, census, index sha, membership range(747) and the final candidate hash against config selection 5db993b1. d.py:147 and p.py:20 refuse without native_unit_regeneration_executed. Omitting the flag also fails, because the selection sha would differ. d.py:119-122 stages u.gz, i.json and m.json from the bundle, checked by sha, to the catalog paths.\n6. LOW, operator. The R1P_PACKET step-2 command block lacks `--unit-binding "$BUN/u.json" --config "$BUN/config.json"`, which appears only in prose at line 65. Copying the block verbatim fails closed but costs a rerun.\n7. PASS, opaque keys. Over the real local audit, the printed breakdown and required_families have no dataset name in any key or value. The map sha ce269588 matches CENSUS_CODES.local.json. The map is in neither the archive nor t.tar. FAIL means unknown*100 > rows, and loader_audit.py:248 raises on it; the tests cover 2/100, 1/99 and 4/4.\n8. LOW, scope of the claim. print_record encodes keys only, so loader_trace lines still print qid values `vsi590k_*`. The local audit has 10 such values; unit traces would print `a0_units_vsi590k_*`. The precedent regex `\\bvsi\\b` misses this token. These lines land in 0700 KH/o and are exempt under 1758Z, but "no dataset name in any printed line" holds only for keys. No unencoded key form such as `scannet_x` occurs today.\n9. PASS, home literal. The embedded source (575ca063) differs from proof 1 only at lines 70 and 72, where /home/jjyeung becomes /home. No /home/<user> appears in the proof script, jb.sh, s.sh or p.py, and the captured argv is clean. I ran the probe on trinity-1-3 with /usr/bin/bwrap and it printed PASS. LOW: `--dir /home` is now a no-op, so the probe no longer mirrors c.sh:346 `--dir /home/jjyeung`. It still tests userns, uid/gid, dev, proc and the read-only /home.\n10. PASS, scope. Config fields that changed: admission path/sha, code path/sha (tree b83a8a35), output, preparation_output, s1_route_policy.table.path (sha unchanged), s1_routing.catalog (+u.gz 14439f0c, i.json 5e4ae8a8, m.json 0d83e137, s.json 5db993b1; old s.json removed), s1_routing.selection path/sha, streams.vqa path/sha (d.json changes only embedded paths), the five routing cents, and type_mix.unit_rows. jb.sh and s.sh are equal to proof 1 apart from the store and run keys, and r.json is byte-equal. BINDING adds unit_binding, sets units_status to BOUND and gains the two absent_on_P unit entries.\n11. PASS, seal and tests. All 44 SHA256SUMS entries are OK; the archive, FIX8.md and FIX8.diff match it. My copy passes all 37 tests (109.6 s, p1cpu Python 3.12).\nNot checked: Orchard staging, production RGB bytes (frame_rates.json says production_authorized=false and frame_bytes_verified=false), production routing populations, and the in-job print output.\n', 'r5.txt': '# GO — archive p_082d2d90.tar sha256 3401c318e552cf0ba23f691d197b8f022550639693632abeeaa3bf3b08658384, config 8246a4dd34bcfb7de1770b62ae7f0f331849714397d66fe68dfda8f8aa676573, run key 07297df8 (delta vs proof 2: 2c67f1f2 / 78d0a06c / p_6f8ed106 def1e1f2)\n1. PASS (scope 1). I flattened both config.json files and found exactly 11 changed leaves. h1.routing_pose_targets false->true is the only semantic change. The ten derived leaves are admission.path/sha256 (v.json carries the new config sha), code.path, output, preparation_output, s1_route_policy.table.path, s1_routing.catalog.<5db993..>, s1_routing.selection.path, and streams.vqa.path/sha256 (in d.json only the bundle prefix changes; the db sha 210b2534.. and source sha 8091154c.. stay equal). S1 is false and both max_own_probability copies are 0.0. type_mix, recipe and scheduled_sampling are equal. Archive members t.tar, u.gz, u.json, m.json, i.json, s.json, selection r/q.json, r.json, j.json, c.json, b0.json, q.py, qp.py, u.py and v.py have the same sha256 as in p_6f8ed106.\n2. PASS (scope 2). One identical validate_switches sits in derive_deployment.py (==archive d.py), seal_proof.py (==archive p.py), out/proof/p.py and the embedded proof; I decompressed p_07297df8.sh and the embedded source has sha 7883e3fe..., equal to proof/p.py. rebind.py imports the same guard. It uses strict `is True`/`is False` and rejects bool, str and None for max_own; NaN, inf and -1 refuse; a missing key or h1 refuses; non-dict input raises, which still fails closed. The guards are tighter than in proof 2: the old checks refused only S1/S2 on, and the old embedded proof had no switch check. Now the embedded proof checks the deployed config at its load boundary. The diff loosens nothing else; jb.sh and s.sh change only paths, job name and run key.\n3. PASS (scope 3). h1.py (a7fd49..), carrier_c1.py (852f19..) and h1_faithful.py are byte-identical to the H1 kit. Rows.get has an equal AST (checked with py3.12). carrier_c1_run.py differs from the kit only by type_mix plumbing (27 diff lines, no h1 code). Routing is not a mix stream, so Rows.get reaches the S2 branch. Only carrier_c1_run.py:1094 and h1.py read the switch, so the sampler does not depend on S2. The kit config d12ae795 ran S2 on the same routing receipt (9a7f3310..).\n4. PASS with limits (scope 3, first batch). On each of 4 ranks, the 10 camera rows (disp 4/dir 3/rot 3) are supervised with pose>0. The 3 absolute-distance rows (the fixture gives them GT) and the 3 units/ft rows have pose 0. All 32 VQA and 8 pointing rows have pose 0. All 16 pose-stream losses per rank are bit-equal to proof 2\'s S2-off first batch. Limit: this shows equal targets and loss at step-1 weights only. It says nothing about later steps, where S2 gradients move the shared pose head; that coupling is intended.\n5. MEDIUM, non-blocking. Every fixture camera row carries GT, and only a unit test covers missing GT. In production, pose_targets masks missing GT silently and has no threshold. Production camera-GT coverage under the vehicle-P selection is unmeasured locally. Before step 100, read h1 pose_supervised and pose_missing per camera type at step 1, and stop if supervised is about 0.\n6. LOW. In tiny_worker, `target_matches_own_frames` is a copy of `supervised` (a tautology). The real checks are the torch.equal against the row\'s gt_pose9 and the frame_indices equality. Pose-to-frame alignment is a property of the store and has no local test.\n7. LOW (labelling). off_sealed.json and off_candidate.json now carry a scope string claiming the "Native S2 target and loss path", but those runs use D0 with S2 off. loader_audit.json was relabelled to 8246a4dd without a rerun; it discloses inherited_sampling_evidence, and per finding 3 the relabel is valid.\n8. INFO (OFF identity). The candidate tree under the D0 config (S1 off, S2 off, both max_own 0) reproduces the sealed D0 tree\'s 4 rank state hashes and matches frozen proof-2 evidence. That covers inert tree changes on a fixture tiny model. It does not cover S2, the deployment gate (which would refuse D0), production RGB or real stores.\n9. INFO. S2 alone (S1 off) has never trained in production; the kit ran S1+S2. The ORCH card already records this as a confound.\n10. PASS (scope 4). The archive sha matches. All entries in out/SHA256SUMS and the archive\'s sums.txt check OK. 43/43 tests pass in my copy (logs/tests2.log) with work/tree extracted from the archived t.tar and the other work/ entries symlinked read-only. The first run had 7 errors because symlink path resolution broke relative_to, an environment artifact. The original snapshots are unmodified (find -newer is empty).\nEvidence: /scratch/jjyeung/orch_n30/review_r1p5/work/{arc,arc_base,logs}; my copies are under review_r1p5/work/snap.\n', 'r6.txt': 'Packet A: p_69d2930d.tar a99ab475f602c63332d4faaa4bf20f9d75e604cb973a80a041338b03a7d5f589 config fac0705214fdecb53561c633d7d94642cd469b50b662c5de81f09d11891d115f (run 673bc60f, S2 on): GO.\nPacket B: p_27bfcd1d.tar 4343e9a08c7b54c745cd5c20b0393d5d222fb5f929b182fe1a3228ae066b5a1a config 0647a0df37862199ea4a766875969d28e7fbfc66821ea5f5a0d00f0607452f92 (run 13daf33c, S2 off): GO.\nReviewer review_r1p6 (trinity-1-3). Scripts and logs are in /scratch/jjyeung/orch_n30/review_r1p6/work/ (recompute.py, cells.py, cdiff.py, tests2_*.log). I found no blocker.\n\n1. PASS. I recomputed the list with the sealed code: _source_lines over store v7 (210b2534, 204,413 rows), then Exclusions(dev, benchmark), the six inherited Removals, and the build_stream predicate against division 0d28fdd4. The predicate refuses exactly 601 rows: 0 duplicate qids, 0 in heldout_scenes, heldout_qids or heldout_group_ids. All 601 are absent from the division (38 scenes; d1 474, d3 127). My (i, qid) set equals FIX10_OFFENDERS.json, and n.json\'s 601 distinct row_keys equal those qids.\n2. PASS. In the full store, n.json matches exactly 601 rows, so it removes no in-division row. Applying all seven lists keeps 203,812 rows with 0 division violations and 0 duplicate qids. The kept rows also clear every held-out list. The format is the sealed one: one nonempty string row_key per line, the pin carries no defects key, and Removals loads it. It matches 0 of the 747 unit rows (packed.jsonl d7c3206c).\n3. INFO. The scene filter and the six inherited lists remove 0 VQA rows from v7, so the new list alone carries the division fix.\n4. PASS. Both bundles carry n.json and records/n.json (02315a74), and sums.txt pins it. BINDING.record_files gains n.json, and d.py stages it at AS+store_key+\'/n.json\'. The fixture derivations\' k/0.json have extra dest .../69d2930d/n.json (A) and .../27bfcd1d/n.json (B) with sha 02315a74. Those paths equal each config\'s appended remove_files pin. jb.sh stages extras read-only (tk_readonly_files), and v.py checks the extra digest.\n5. PASS. The proof fails closed. pinned() raises "Missing or changed pinned input" for a missing file and for a one-line-changed file; I ran both cases.\n6. PASS. Config A against 8246a4dd and B against 2c67f1f2 differ only in: the appended remove_files pin (the six-entry prefix is byte-equal), room 172->170, direction 3117->3119, and derived paths and keys (admission/v.json, code.path, output, preparation_output, s1 route/selection paths, streams.vqa path and sha). The new d.json differs from the old only in path prefixes: database 210b2534, division 0d28fdd4 and source 8091154c are unchanged.\n7. PASS. Both configs set S1 (h1.faithful_own_camera_rows) false and both max_own_probability values to 0.0. h1.routing_pose_targets (S2) is true in A and false in B. tree_sha256 is b83a8a35 for both, the code archive is e5be8157, and the trainer tree equals the sealed tree (diff -rq clean). Packet members changed only in derived files plus n.json.\n8. PASS. Cells: my family counts over the 203,812 rows equal FIX10_CELLS.json for all 18 families. Every cell satisfies cents <= floor(400 x eligible / 1000); room 170 = cap 170 at 425 eligible. The sealed type_mix.allocate, given the old cells and the new counts, yields exactly the config cells (room 170, direction 3119; sum 12,800). With the new cells it makes no cut and no refill.\n9. PASS. Both archive shas equal the brief and SHA256SUMS. sha256sum -c is 160/160 OK for A and 104/104 OK for B.\n10. PASS. In my copies (sealed tree copied in, CUDA hidden), the tests ran 61 for A and 61 for B: all OK, including test_fix10\'s full-store build with and without the list.\n11. LOW (B only). The B bundle\'s d.py and p.py also change against 2c67f1f2. They replace "switches must be off" with A\'s validate_switches, which adds the max_own==0 check. The change is stricter only, and the config passes it. It is not part of the REMOVE delta.\n12. RISK, not a blocker. The local replay does not