ind work/tmp /tmp, where work=/tmp/jjyeung/p_673bc60f_<job> is fresh and checked empty, so the outer writable mounts and the temporary_paths check stay unchanged. The inner bind has the same form as admission's, which ran in 170956 (rc=0), and the directory_modes walk passed there after admission.\n3. PASS (R1_RUNTIME_RECORD). The sha comes from tk_current record in pinned k/0.json. sha_is checks $S/c7d31ddd/anyhost/<sha>.json, which admission's tk_stage writes and sha-checks (c.sh:302-306) before any mode branch. The exported $P/... path is visible through --ro-bind $S/c7d31ddd $P. If tk_current fails, read returns 1 at EOF and set -e aborts, so sha_is never sees an empty sha.\n4. INFO. TK_RUNS_DIR=$NR=/tmp/jjyeung/a_673bc60f/runs, the parent of launch run_directory, so it equals r.sh:40's value. Sealed c.sh never reads it (NR is constant at c.sh:22), and no trainer .py reads it either.\n5. PASS (only the proof changed). Both archives have 37 members with identical tar headers except p_673bc60f.sh (9094->9310 B) and sums.txt, which differs in that one line. t.tar (trainer plus c.sh/r.sh/p0.sh), config.json, BINDING.json, jb.sh, s.sh, p.py (seal_proof), d.py, v.py, q.py, qp.py, u.*, b0.json, records/* and the selection files are byte-equal. Between the snapshots, tools differ only in make_proof.py (the 8 program lines) and package_operator.py (archive naming), and tests add test_fix11 plus one import in test_packet. config.json, r1p_code.tar, units/ and records/ are byte-equal. The derivation kits derive_ewm1__cr/a and derive_uzp4u2px/a are diff -rq clean (c.sh, r.sh, p0.sh, job.sh, a.py/d.py admission predicates, SHA256SUMS.txt).\n6. PASS (archive name). The bundle and kit tokens come from BINDING.store_key (69d2930d), which is unchanged. s.sh, jb.sh, ids.json and sums.txt name only i_69d2930d and x_69d2930d, and no member names the archive. Only OPERATOR.json, which is local and unshipped (production_authorized=false), records the archive name. The authority's bundle_files pins p_673bc60f.sh, so the old authority fails closed on the new script; deployment must copy p_a5dc8f30.tar and reseal against the deployed kit (RESEAL11 covers only a local fixture). s.sh's go.json gate binds the wrapper sha and kit manifest, and both are unchanged.\n7. RISK (fixture scope). The fixture stubs admission (r.sh), bwrap (a Python argument parser that asserts sources exist, with no namespace and no ro enforcement), the loader body, python (/usr/bin/python3) and the k/0.json entries. It remaps S U NX NR X AS AL P EPOCHS after sourcing and skips the wrapper and job prefixes, which 170956 already ran. It therefore does NOT prove real loader_audit success (required_families, prefix_check, disk_plan), that $X/runs/673bc60f/inputs is writable inside the inner namespace, or that the caller's nested user namespace works; admission's identical tk_bwrap/tk_env set ran in production, which mitigates the last two.\n8. RISK (walltime). The proof runs at -t 04:00:00, and 170956 had used 2:41:58 when admission ended. Unless admission gets faster, the loader audit and the receipt write have about 1 h 18 min. The caller also skips r.sh's p-mode thread exports (OMP/MKL up to 16, STUDENT_IO_THREADS=16), so the audit runs with OMP_NUM_THREADS=1. This affects speed only, not -u.\n9. PASS (shas, tests). The archive sha equals SHA256SUMS line 108. sha256sum -c fails only the 4 files that r1_ops3's rerun regenerated (logs/finalize.log, POST_ADMISSION_SHELL, PRE_SUBMISSION, RESEAL11), as FREEZE_NOTE says; none is an archive member. The script's embedded blob decodes to sha b7ce4ec9, byte-equal to out/proof/p.py. In my copy, test_fix11 passed 7/7 (sealed c.sh, both NumPy branches, all mutants refused). fix8, fix9, fix10, derivation_pre_submit and test_packet did not run in my copy: they need the packet's work/ (work/reference/...), which I may not copy, and student_pilot in subprocesses. I rely on r1_ops3's chk11_*_b.log (all OK) and RLC_RC=0 for those.\n10. INFO. SHA256SUMS no longer lists p_69d2930d.tar; FIX11_PROTECTED_ARCHIVES.json still pins it.\n", 'r8.txt': "Packet A: p_9dd2fbb7.tar 9dd2fbb77503ecee875d538ebaed933cc95ff286f76e5955fc2591f63e3f0192 config fac0705214fdecb53561c633d7d94642cd469b50b662c5de81f09d11891d115f (run 673bc60f, S2 on, canary gate): GO.\nReviewer review_r1p8 (trinity-1-3, Devin Opus high). Work: /scratch/jjyeung/orch_n30/review_r1p8/ (tmp/{old,new,f11} extracted archives, copy/, t_*.log). GO carries the operator conditions in 3 and 4; no code fix is needed before launch.\n1. PASS (two modes only). CANARY runs only when go.json `canary` is JSON `true` (s.sh:27, `is True`). Every other value takes the else branch, which holds the old lines 27-38 re-indented with the text unchanged (diff old/new s.sh). The five GO checks (s.sh:24-25) and the sbatch line (s.sh:109) are unchanged. Every refusal raises inside the heredoc, so python exits non-zero and `set -e` stops before sbatch. `env -u PYTHONOPTIMIZE python3 -I` keeps the asserts live. ADMISSION_JOB is ignored in PASS mode. Any missing file or key raises (read_bytes, KeyError). squeue runs with check=True and must return exactly one row in PENDING or RUNNING, so a missing job, a queue error, or a COMPLETED/FAILED/COMPLETING job refuses.\n2. PASS (evidence chain on the real bytes). The local copies are receipt 164ef356 and log 911729ca. The log has one line, `2026-11-18T00:27:16Z | exit rc=0`, and the gate's regex returns ['0']. The receipt carries identity fac07052 and contract 6511a329, and its selection equals the config's s1_routing.selection (5db993b1). The log's 7 REMOVE pins equal the config's remove_files exactly, n.json 02315a74 included. The receipt's own status FAIL/rc 1 is not consulted, which is correct for this mode.\n3. MEDIUM (operator condition: job-name collision). The proof and the training job both run as a15_cot_ap673bc60f (s.sh:84 and :109). No kit file writes BUN/job.id; s.sh:31 only reads it. Input that gets through: job.id = PROOF_JOB = the id of an already RUNNING training job. That launches a second training job with no proof. Condition: write job.id only from the proof's `sbatch --parsable` output, and record in the launch event that squeue shows PROOF_JOB at time limit 4:00:00 with no gres. Later round: make the gate check `%l` or `%b`.\n4. LOW (operator condition). A held PENDING proof (JobHeldUser, DependencyNeverSatisfied) passes the gate, and kill rule (b) needs the proof to run. Record squeue `%r` for the proof in the launch event.\n5. LOW (marker). The gate writes KH/o/<PROOF_JOB>.canary.json with mode `x` after a.main and before sbatch, in the same directory as the job's %j.err, where later readers look. The marker holds no training job id, and jb.sh is unchanged, so the run's own records do not say canary. Record the sbatch job id beside the marker path in the launch event. If sbatch fails, the marker stays GATE_ACCEPTED and blocks a retry with the same PROOF_JOB (fail-closed). Rename the marker in that case; do not delete it.\n6. PASS (diff table). I extracted both archives: of 37 members, only p_673bc60f.sh, s.sh and sums.txt differ. p_673bc60f.sh is b3c6c231, the same file as in fix 11's p_a5dc8f30.tar; against a5dc8f30, only s.sh and sums.txt differ. In diff12_ecu8i7of, `diff -rq old_kit new_kit` is clean over 99 files. The authorities differ only in bundle_files.s.sh and bundle_files.p_673bc60f.sh. t.tar (trainer, c.sh, r.sh, p0.sh), jb.sh, config.json, BINDING.json, ids.json and the rest are byte-equal, so the admission predicates are unchanged. KIT_DIFF12.md matches all of this.\n7. PASS (TK_JOBDIR carry-over). The embedded proof decodes to b7ce4ec9ba56eceac21d5b246914e78aeac2d3a37901f07610a620f64d2140ff. That is byte-equal to review_r1p7's embedded_p.py and to out/proof/p.py, and PROOF_DIFF12.diff shows only the fix-11 lines. test_fix11 passes 7/7 in my copy (t_test_fix11b.log), including the post-admission nounset replay. POST_ADMISSION_SHELL.json reads status PASS, proof b7ce4ec9, c.sh 900d0535.\n8. PASS (shas, tests). The archive sha equals SHA256SUMS line 119, and `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS` gives 179/179 OK. test_fix12 passes 14/14 in my copy (t_test_fix12.log). Two test_fix11 cases first errored because the brief forbids copying p_*.tar; they pass once I symlinked the archives read-only. Not run: the full 67-test suite (fix8/9/10, test_packet and derivation need work/), so I rely on r1_pkt/out/logs/tests.log (Ran 67, OK) and fix12_gate_tests.log (14 OK).\n9. RISK (not executed). The Orchard evidence chain has not run anywhere. The old kit must be renamed to x_69d2930d.f170956 and keep SHA256SUMS.txt (4617dc08), k/18fccf83.json, k/0.json (646efd43), b/c.sh and o/170956.proof.{json,log}. The gate fails closed if any of them is missing. The walltime risk in R1P7 item 8 (4 h proof) still applies.\n10. INFO (content scan). The visible surface is not byte-equal, so ruling item 2's quick scan is still owed. My read of the s.sh additions found only tokens that the scanned kit already contains (`.split` in d.py/p.py/u.py, `vqa` in config.json/q.py), plus paths and environment names listed in KIT_DIFF12. This was not a formal scan.\n", 'rc1.txt': "Packet C: p_c60b9015.tar c60b901594843989b909cb785a5fdc9ad544ea0fdec8d78c63bf173e4f6e136c config 6594f46cdc16168514aca26a6ce38285907adfc6ece0b75d8e10428ea0b2fe74 (run 05b8ac69, continuation of A at step 200): GO.\nReviewer review_r1c1 (Devin Opus, trinity-1-3). Copy and extracts: /scratch/jjyeung/orch_n30/review_r1c1/{c,tmp/x (C),tmp/a (A)}. No refutation of items 1-4 held up; the risks below are all fail-closed or have no effect on training.\n1. PASS (resume): b/c0.py pins PARENT fac07052, RUN 673bc60f and STEP 200. It takes only a verified A/B slot at step 200 (content_check c1-slot-check-v1, the same fields A's jb.sh put_record writes). It checks archive bytes and SHA while streaming, accepts only regular members, and requires binding.json equal to A's mirror and complete.json equal to the slot